 "description": "Tunes for Formant Singer by style: choir, solo voices, bass voices, whisper and breath, pads and ambient, cinematic, pop leads, robot and FX, chant, lullaby, hymn and syllable study. Every tune is a complete voice with a short original text (about 2 to 9 syllables, in English, Dutch or phonemes) that fits the style. The text expects one note per syllable: a chord counts as one note, and the text starts again after the last syllable. Syllables per text: Choir 4 to 5; Solo Voices 4 to 7; Bass Voices 1 to 4; Whisper and Breath 3 to 6; Pads and Ambient 1 to 4; Cinematic 1 to 6; Pop Leads 4 to 6; Robot and FX 2 to 5; Chant 4 to 6; Lullaby 3 to 7; Hymn 2 to 9; Syllable Study 6 to 8. Tunes with a fixed vowel sing that one vowel on every note. Play a melody with that many notes (the card shows the current syllable); press Restart to start the text again.",
